# Root-level catch-all. Each app also has its own .gitignore for
# language-specific ignores (apps/api/.gitignore, apps/web/.gitignore).
#
# NOTE: adding a path here does NOT untrack a file that is already in the
# index — gitignore only applies to untracked paths. Both entries below
# were listed here AND tracked anyway for several commits; use
# `git rm -r --cached <path>` to actually stop tracking something.
.DS_Store
*.log

# graphify's generated index/cache — regenerable, not source.
graphify-out/

# impeccable skill's local hook cache — regenerable, not source.
.impeccable/

# --- Repo-wide heavy/generated directories ---------------------------------
#
# These are ALSO covered by the per-app .gitignore files, and that was not
# enough. `npm install` in apps/web ran before apps/web/.gitignore existed,
# leaving a window where 12,559 node_modules files were genuinely untracked
# — long enough for an editor to cache that count and keep showing it. Root
# patterns close the window and cover any app added later.
#
# For scale, these account for ~25,000 ignored files: node_modules ~12.5k,
# .venv ~10.6k, .mypy_cache ~1.8k. `git status` correctly reports 0; a tool
# that counts ignored files reports 25k. Both numbers are right about
# different questions.
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Tool caches
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tsbuildinfo
*.tsbuildinfo

# Build output
dist/
build/
